```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "ts-consign-service",
      "fault_kind": "database_call_slow",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT t, service_name, span_name, count(*) n, round(avg(duration)/1e6,1) avg_ms, round(quantile_cont(duration,0.9)/1e6,1) p90_ms FROM (SELECT 'a' t, * FROM abnormal_traces UNION ALL SELECT 'n', * FROM normal_traces) WHERE service_name='ts-consign-service' AND span_name IN ('SELECT ts.consign_record','INSERT ts.consign_record') GROUP BY ALL ORDER BY 3,1",
          "claim": "Consign's own DB client spans (SELECT/INSERT ts.consign_record) rose from about 1ms normal to about 1.2-1.8s abnormal."
        },
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT t, span_name, count(*) n, round(avg(duration)/1e6,1) avg_ms, round(quantile_cont(duration,0.9)/1e6,1) p90_ms FROM (SELECT 'a' t, * FROM abnormal_traces UNION ALL SELECT 'n', * FROM normal_traces) WHERE service_name='ts-ui-dashboard' AND attr_span_kind='Server' AND span_name LIKE '%consignservice/consigns/account%' GROUP BY ALL ORDER BY 2,1",
          "claim": "User-facing consigns/account requests through ui-dashboard went from about 9ms normal to about 3.3s abnormal."
        },
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT c.service_name, ch.service_name callee, count(*) n, round(avg(c.duration)/1e6,1) caller_ms, round(avg(ch.duration)/1e6,1) child_ms FROM abnormal_traces c JOIN abnormal_traces ch ON ch.parent_span_id=c.span_id AND ch.trace_id=c.trace_id WHERE c.service_name='ts-consign-service' AND c.attr_span_kind='Client' GROUP BY ALL",
          "claim": "Consign's DB spans are client spans with no downstream service child, so the slowdown sits inside consign's own database calls."
        },
        {
          "kind": "metric",
          "sql": "SELECT t, attr_source, attr_destination, count(*) n, round(avg(value),1) avg_v FROM (SELECT 'a' t,* FROM abnormal_metrics_sum UNION ALL SELECT 'n',* FROM normal_metrics_sum) WHERE metric='hubble_tcp_flags_total' AND (attr_source LIKE '%consign-service%' AND attr_destination LIKE '%mysql%') GROUP BY ALL ORDER BY 1",
          "claim": "Network flow counters between consign and mysql-0 are essentially unchanged from normal, so the network is not the cause."
        },
        {
          "kind": "log",
          "sql": "SELECT service_name, level, substr(message,1,200) msg, count(*) n FROM abnormal_logs WHERE service_name='ts-consign-service' AND level='SEVERE' GROUP BY ALL",
          "claim": "Consign logs SEVERE dispatcher exceptions from duplicate-row query results during the incident window."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "service": "ts-seat-service",
      "fault_kind": "http_slow",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT ch.service_name callee, count(*) n, round(avg(c.duration)/1e6,1) caller_ms, round(avg(ch.duration)/1e6,1) child_server_ms FROM abnormal_traces c JOIN abnormal_traces ch ON ch.parent_span_id=c.span_id AND ch.trace_id=c.trace_id WHERE c.service_name='ts-seat-service' AND c.attr_span_kind='Client' AND ch.attr_span_kind='Server' GROUP BY ALL ORDER BY 1",
          "claim": "Seat's outgoing HTTP client spans to config and order services are much slower than the callee server spans they wrap."
        },
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT CAST(floor((epoch(time)-1755133600)/60) AS INT) min_b, count(*) n, round(avg(duration)/1e6,1) avg_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='ts-seat-service' AND attr_span_kind='Server' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1",
          "claim": "Seat's own server latency steps up from about 17ms to 65-95ms after roughly two minutes into the incident."
        },
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT t, service_name, span_name, count(*) n, round(avg(duration)/1e6,1) avg_ms FROM (SELECT 'a' t,* FROM abnormal_traces UNION ALL SELECT 'n',* FROM normal_traces) WHERE service_name='ts-seat-service' AND attr_span_kind='Client' GROUP BY ALL ORDER BY 3,1",
          "claim": "Seat's outgoing GET and POST client spans rose from about 5ms normal to about 13ms abnormal."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "propagation": [
    {
      "from": "ts-consign-service",
      "to": "ts-ui-dashboard",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT c.service_name caller, ch.service_name callee, count(*) n, round(avg(c.duration)/1e6,1) caller_ms, round(avg(ch.duration)/1e6,1) child_ms FROM abnormal_traces c JOIN abnormal_traces ch ON ch.parent_span_id=c.span_id AND ch.trace_id=c.trace_id WHERE c.service_name='ts-ui-dashboard' AND ch.service_name='ts-consign-service' AND c.attr_span_kind='Client' GROUP BY ALL",
          "claim": "ui-dashboard's client calls to consign-service take about as long as consign's server spans, so consign's latency passes straight to the user-facing dashboard."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "from": "ts-seat-service",
      "to": "ts-travel-service",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT c.service_name caller, ch.service_name callee, CAST(floor((epoch(c.time)-1755133600)/60) AS INT) min_b, count(*) n, round(avg(c.duration)/1e6,1) caller_ms, round(avg(ch.duration)/1e6,1) child_ms FROM abnormal_traces c JOIN abnormal_traces ch ON ch.parent_span_id=c.span_id AND ch.trace_id=c.trace_id WHERE c.service_name='ts-travel-service' AND ch.service_name='ts-seat-service' GROUP BY ALL ORDER BY 3",
          "claim": "Travel's calls to seat take longer over time, tracking seat's slowdown, with travel's own trip-detail latency rising alongside."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "from": "ts-seat-service",
      "to": "ts-preserve-service",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT c.service_name caller, ch.service_name callee, count(*) n, round(avg(c.duration)/1e6,1) caller_ms, round(avg(ch.duration)/1e6,1) child_ms FROM abnormal_traces c JOIN abnormal_traces ch ON ch.parent_span_id=c.span_id AND ch.trace_id=c.trace_id WHERE c.service_name='ts-preserve-service' AND ch.service_name='ts-seat-service' GROUP BY ALL",
          "claim": "Preserve's calls to seat show inflated caller-side time versus seat's server spans, adding latency to the preserve flow."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "from": "ts-travel-service",
      "to": "ts-route-plan-service",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT c.service_name caller, ch.service_name callee, count(*) n, round(avg(c.duration)/1e6,1) caller_ms, round(avg(ch.duration)/1e6,1) child_ms FROM abnormal_traces c JOIN abnormal_traces ch ON ch.parent_span_id=c.span_id AND ch.trace_id=c.trace_id WHERE c.service_name='ts-route-plan-service' AND ch.service_name='ts-travel-service' GROUP BY ALL",
          "claim": "Route-plan's calls into travel-service run about 20-30ms slower in the incident period, passing travel's latency upstream."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "from": "ts-route-plan-service",
      "to": "ts-travel-plan-service",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT c.service_name caller, ch.service_name callee, count(*) n, round(avg(c.duration)/1e6,1) caller_ms, round(avg(ch.duration)/1e6,1) child_ms FROM abnormal_traces c JOIN abnormal_traces ch ON ch.parent_span_id=c.span_id AND ch.trace_id=c.trace_id WHERE c.service_name='ts-travel-plan-service' AND ch.service_name='ts-route-plan-service' GROUP BY ALL",
          "claim": "Travel-plan's calls to route-plan take about 415ms abnormal versus about 298ms normal, carrying the slowdown upstream."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "from": "ts-travel-plan-service",
      "to": "ts-ui-dashboard",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT span_name, count(*) n, round(avg(duration)/1e6,1) avg_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='ts-ui-dashboard' AND attr_span_kind='Server' AND span_name LIKE '%travelplanservice%' GROUP BY 1",
          "claim": "The travel-plan endpoints reached through ui-dashboard are slower, about 0.5-1s, reaching the user-facing tier."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "from": "ts-preserve-service",
      "to": "ts-ui-dashboard",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT c.service_name caller, ch.service_name callee, count(*) n, round(avg(c.duration)/1e6,1) caller_ms, round(avg(ch.duration)/1e6,1) child_ms FROM abnormal_traces c JOIN abnormal_traces ch ON ch.parent_span_id=c.span_id AND ch.trace_id=c.trace_id WHERE c.service_name='ts-ui-dashboard' AND ch.service_name='ts-preserve-service' GROUP BY ALL",
          "claim": "Ui-dashboard's preserve calls take about 720ms abnormal, nearly all of it inside preserve, versus about 270ms normal."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

**Caveat:** `ts-seat-service` (http_slow) is moderately confident. Its outgoing calls inflate while the callee server spans stay normal. Propagation edges from seat are partly inferred from call structure and timing, not a single direct trace.

**Not named:** Services such as basic, route, price, station, train and several others show a milder slowdown from roughly the same time, alongside slightly slower DB spans across many services. I could not attribute that to a specific fault in this telemetry, so I left it out.
